<section class="view show"><section class="card"><div class="cardHead"><b>Branch transfer balances</b><span>Posted branch payouts</span></div><div class="cardBody"><p class="tiny">A receiving branch uses its own verified cash to pay the receiver. The sending branch owes that amount; the receiving branch records it as due from the sending office. Reconcile these dues against actual branch settlement. They are separate from cash, customer deposits and transfer fees.</p><div class="tableWrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Branch</th><th>Currency</th><th>Due from branches</th><th>Due to branches</th></tr></thead><tbody><% if(!data.rows.length){ %><tr><td colspan="4">No posted cross-branch dues in this viewing scope.</td></tr><% } %><% data.rows.forEach(row=>{ %><tr><td><%= row.branch %></td><td><%= row.currency %></td><td><%= row.receivable %></td><td><%= row.payable %></td></tr><% }) %></tbody></table></div></div></section></section>